Subject: [PATCH 5/5] =?UTF-8?q?api:=20EnsureVethWire=20=E2=80=94=20idempot?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ent=20veth=20wires=20with=20symmetric=20owner=20alias?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extend the vxlan ownership concept to veth wires. A logical link is
identified by a symmetric IFLA_IFALIAS ('meshnet:veth:<topo-ns>:<link-uid>',
via VethWireAlias) that BOTH directions derive identically, so either side
can recognize a wire the other side already realized.

EnsureVethWire(local, peer, alias) replaces check-then-MakeVeth callers:

- adopt: if both slots hold the two ends of one structurally verified veth
  pair (kernel peer-ifindex reciprocity via ethtool, evaluated inside each
  namespace) — or both carry our alias when verification is unavailable —
  the wire is correct no matter who created it: refresh aliases, bring both
  ends up, re-add addresses (EEXIST-tolerant), succeed.
- recreate: absent ends, halves of broken pairs, and alias-less or
  koko-vxlan leftovers occupying topology-owned names are deleted and the
  pair is created fresh, then tagged on both ends.
- conflict: a slot owned by a DIFFERENT meshnet wire alias fails loudly
  (two links claiming one ifname is a topology error). Cosmetic aliases a
  NOS may set (interface descriptions) never block.

Safety and concurrency:
- eth0/lo/empty names are refused outright: the delegated CNI interface is
  never created, deleted or re-owned here.
- All creators serialize behind the node-wide wire-create lock (shared with
  MakeVxLan), making inspect-then-act atomic among koko actors; a bounded
  re-inspect loop (3 attempts, backoff) absorbs races with anything else.
- Namespace probes wrap failures in NamespaceGoneError so callers can park
  a link (peer sandbox being recreated) instead of failing a whole CNI ADD.

The decision core (decideEnsureVeth) is a pure function with a unit-test
truth table. Upstreamable.
